swer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186196295}] :answer-field/id #uuid "8ae68f40-20e6-597a-a9b7-9dac54c3c828" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186196290}] :question/id #uuid "587a7a92-f47b-5043-840d-bba7363fe179" :question/math-academy-id "q-183495" :question/problem "$P(x)$: $6 \\mid x$ $Q(x)$: $3 \\mid x$\n\nConsider the predicates $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ above. Which of the following expresses the conditional predicate $P(x)⇒Q(x)$?\n\n1. $6 \\mid x$ is sufficient for $3 \\mid x$\n2. For $3 \\mid x$, it is sufficient that $6 \\mid x$\n3. $6 \\mid x$ is necessary for $3 \\mid x$\n4. For $6 \\mid x$, it is necessary that $3 \\mid x$"}]}
